# The SolidWorks appearance library under native/crates/cad-ir/assets.
#
# The 619 `.p2m` files are 332 KB of text, are compiled into the crate by
# build.rs and are the only statement of how a finish looks — they belong in
# the repository. The images beside them are 935 MB of textures, HDR
# environments and thumbnails that the converter never opens; a `.p2m` names
# them by a path inside a SolidWorks installation and nothing here resolves it.
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/Images/
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.jpg
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.png
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.dds
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.hdr
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.bmp
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.tif
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.rgb
native/crates/cad-ir/assets/**/*.xml

# The native libraries staged for the NuGet package, and the packages
# themselves. Both are build output: `dotnet/pack.sh` rebuilds the first and
# produces the second, and a copy checked in is a copy that goes stale.
runtimes/
dist/

# Render evidence. Generated, not source.
renders/

# Siemens' own XT format reference, if you keep a copy here. It is their
# document, not ours to redistribute; docs/parasolid-xt-notes.md says where to
# get it.
docs/xt-reference.md
